{"answers":[{"available_context":{"messages":[{"id":"m2120","original_text_sha256":"58254259502f4442a1bbf45ecd0f32d020725c80b6dfbfaadce4a656d402192e","redacted":false,"role":"user","source_line":2120,"source_message_id":"ed9d7e3b-f0a4-493e-81aa-fc8e4e2e185b","text":"Add small init to packages/cli. It writes a small.toml in the current directory from what it can detect, so a user never has to know the file format.

Detection uses the existing entry-and-framework logic from deploy: find the entry file by hints then filename convention, sniff the framework, and check for requirements.txt. Then write:

toml
name = "<directory name, slugified>"
entry = "<detected>"
framework = "<detected>"

[deps]
file = "requirements.txt"      # only if it exists

[secrets]
required = []                  # env vars this app reads — fill in

[access]
visibility = "domain"

Print every decision on its own line (✓ entry: app.py (flask)). If the entry can't be determined, write the file anyway with entry = "" and a comment, then exit 1 with one line telling the user what to fill in.

Also scan the entry file for os.environ[...], os.getenv(...), and os.environ.get(...) and pre-fill [secrets] required with those names. That's the single most useful thing this command can do.

Never overwrite an existing small.toml — print that it exists and exit 0. Add --force to overwrite.

Make small deploy call init automatically when no small.toml is present, so the common path is still one command.

Update skills/small/SKILL.md: the agent runs small init first, then fills in anything marked "fill in", then small deploy.

